<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Scientists discover quasar formed 630 million years after the Big Bang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:575ecaa408728b810cb463bc08157a4fc7f49fa0a364cb5edc8e26f92df2aa4b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T22:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-quasar-formed-630-million-years-after-the-big-bang/a-80041882--1abb7e69693f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-quasar-formed-630-million-years-after-the-big-bang/a-80041882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Scientists are seeing the quasar as it was 13.1 billion years ago — when the universe was less than 5% of its current age.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European court finds states can turn back migrants in some cases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca6de35fa0cdc79590b0e8ffb081df86802fb9689868ade01597bc65627581c9</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T17:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-court-finds-states-can-turn-back-migrants-in-some-cases/a-80038352--8cb11e591c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-court-finds-states-can-turn-back-migrants-in-some-cases/a-80038352?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe's top human rights court ruled that member states can turn back migrants unless they've been identified as people who were at risk of suffering.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy and Hungary's Magyar meet amid thaw in ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cbcdf0febaaa1ded3097fb065291b926a58cf7caa1bc985590dac0da870d26c</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-and-hungary-s-magyar-meet-amid-thaw-in-ties/a-80036546--06399634af9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-and-hungary-s-magyar-meet-amid-thaw-in-ties/a-80036546?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar has arrived in Ukraine for meetings with President Volodymyr Zelenskyy and ethnic Hungarians. Both leaders say they want better relations after a change of leadership in Budapest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dd952b801c7e8fb632e7545d5f14c57256b01ee951dc7e23007b1d26c9ef5d5</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>HIV infections could rise amid aid cuts, UN warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1b7456c0421c53f5b2930cc44b2269cc6f2f0fc19a410118112e9965fbaf451</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hiv-infections-could-rise-amid-aid-cuts-un-warns/a-80036263--c28a069d7c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hiv-infections-could-rise-amid-aid-cuts-un-warns/a-80036263?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The impact of United States government funding cuts has been dramatic for many HIV programs, UNAIDS warned. The agency expects that 2027 data to show an increase in new infections after being on the cusp of ending AIDS.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Francis diaries recount spiritual crisis, him seeing the 'Devil'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94dfb47986032b1fec4b9e934c2d13ab4bd75e64b4a1154ac580fe8f6f1cec15</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-francis-diaries-recount-spiritual-crisis-him-seeing-the-devil/a-80033224--d366e3ee18f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-francis-diaries-recount-spiritual-crisis-him-seeing-the-devil/a-80033224?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Extracts of the late Pope Francis' diaries have been published, the first release of its kind since the 1960s. They discuss his struggles with his role in the Vatican and visions of the devil and the gates of hell.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: Why do some EU member states use their vetoes to block the accession of certain candidate countries?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5afd0a5f95bbd5213dcd012cecb7ec50462f2873471720670414ae753b44e9a7</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candi/a-80034401--27cd622204d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candidate-countries/a-80034401?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Individual EU member states use their veto powers to block candidate countries in the accession process — often for reasons of domestic politics. DW takes a look at some cases and examines what's behind them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CAS reinstates Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b1a633aa7e6eeb6c2f4ade52359e2d79c69d7558254882336db8a3dd3a95600</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027--561a21777065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has reinstated Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions, overturning a CAF decision that stripped them of the title. Morocco, previously declared winners, are confirmed runners-up.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why Iran's medicine supply chain is failing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90057fe943727e76f3b84912a25814155bb285aa721e0a33f11cc3307e93e86d</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-iran-s-medicine-supply-chain-is-failing/a-80035268--b9206162e8f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-iran-s-medicine-supply-chain-is-failing/a-80035268?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pharmacies in Iran are closing, hospital deliveries have stalled and patients are rationing doses or turning to black markets.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Colombia: Car bomb attack injures at least 23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b25519988d17fd825aa22db61c8b554850a2489b9f4fd096595cd59b552ec56</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/colombia-car-bomb-attack-injures-at-least-23/a-80033956--057490e4a70f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/colombia-car-bomb-attack-injures-at-least-23/a-80033956?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion in Villavicencio coincides with the tenth anniversary of a peace accord with FARC guerrillas, casting doubt on Colombia's peace process.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Wadephul 'shocked' by Trump's Nvidia intervention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7480e540db90d14bcb39b3e95bd466b89023b8d86fd0877cab5d7baf1a6653a6</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954--71b26658a53e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German foreign minister has criticized Donald Trump's interference in the chip-maker's economic activities. Jensen Huang was brought back after stepping down as Nvidia CEO amid multiple scandals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Land mine deaths reach five-year high, watchdog says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5340498a483ad7d8abf8545776e660ab5c6b7c3e39676c8031e74ffa5ae0f959</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/land-mine-deaths-reach-five-year-high-watchdog-says/a-80033092--0de8441f0e99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/land-mine-deaths-reach-five-year-high-watchdog-says/a-80033092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Myanmar reported the highest annual land mine casualty toll, followed by Syria and Afghanistan, ICBL report says. Since 1999, nearly 50 thousand people were killed by land mines.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is North Korea holding back on sending Russia more troops?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d76ffda4f9f75035b29eaaa531ff1c4369fa2404173ff7fb588cd4b087d32d7</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025--db490ffc00f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A North Korean troop buildup Ukraine warned about months ago has yet to materialize, even as strategic cooperation continues. Analysts say Pyongyang is balancing its ties with Moscow and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Five women killed every hour by family members or partners — UN report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a003fb0fb5868f8fe3ba6409fa36f5920f1452fccf3f8cffe551a113602c3b5</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-women-killed-every-hour-by-family-members-or-partners-un-report/a-80030010--891b4a94f505.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-women-killed-every-hour-by-family-members-or-partners-un-report/a-80030010?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On average, 129 women or girls were killed every day in 2025 by someone in their close social circle, UN data showed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bombed factories, billion-dollar opportunity: Why German companies are staying in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e840a2aff0650840426b298709795dfacc0e7e38cf5049010fdc686d1ab166</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201--13f674deb921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German companies remain committed to Ukraine despite million-dollar losses, an unreliable energy supply and a shortage of skilled workers. They are betting on new markets and long-term growth.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How cautious investors are struggling to avoid the AI bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8adb08b37f2a854f7bd5cac7191843243e6cd0224468ace3f0be8fd2769c1d14</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412--863307befc9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-cautious-investors-are-struggling-to-avoid-the-ai-bubble/a-80016412?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Nvidia to Coreweave, AI and tech stocks have swung sharply in recent months. Some investors still see plenty of room to run, while others are trying to diversify — and finding it harder than expected.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU imposes import quotas for hybrid vehicles from China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:699fc52a4b4373569907a976c9111c04b195e51ffb2b5afdc3ea37bd6e8aeebb</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981--7d148967ab4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is trying to protect its own car manufacturers from what it called "overcapacity" in China. Carmakers in the bloc, especially in Germany, have been lagging behind their Chinese rivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German directors' doc on stolen film wins International Emmy Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c882fc7dda1c4399fa64a7f549fb1e41d9d9b4a416cbdda2c9b833fc03972921</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455--80792ca0c998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two German film students confronted the American who won festival prizes with their animated movie. "The Talented Mr. F," their documentary on their fight against plagiarism, is now in the spotlight.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Istanbul 'lion hunt' ends with no big cat found after all</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e380209cb8ee4d7b1482bb4897b8b96f6a332673fef23839798ae70ca838a4d3</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/istanbul-lion-hunt-ends-with-no-big-cat-found-after-all/a-80020913--fa598e50bf7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/istanbul-lion-hunt-ends-with-no-big-cat-found-after-all/a-80020913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a major search operation for a lion on the loose in Istanbul woodlands, Turkish authorities said "the animal was neither a lion nor any other big cat."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistani astronaut to join Chinese space mission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef2636e8c2e3d69eca5ed74f0d59a570bfa66846154a838757e2f5a909697c85</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922--3c985eac77fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani astronaut is set to become to the first foreigner to board China's Tiangong space station. Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, a payload specialist, will join the Shenzhou-24 mission when it launches on Wednesday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese official gets death sentence in spy case, report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93be140b88ece033844501d48f628f7f3ee5bd91e6d241449f2321aa28ac5544</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393--388878bff1dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese official recruited while working abroad was paid more than a million yuan to leak secrets, state-affiliated media reported.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
